fixtures**: Both seeded and unseeded fixtures share the same decomposer biomass (0.1g) so that TAN generation rates are equal; they differ only in nitrifier biomass and maturity, isolating the cycling variable.\n- **ProcessParams extended with serde(default)**: All new fields in `ProcessParamsPreset` use `#[serde(default)]` so existing TOML files without the new fields still load correctly.\n- **CleanFilter biomass setback**: Intensity-proportional setback (50% of intensity) applied to all four microbial guild biomasses (decomposer, AOB, NOB, comammox).\n\n## Spec Deviations\n- **`dissolved_feed_residue_g_total` is bookkeeping only**: The spec mentions an \"equivalent short-lived leach pool\" — we use `dissolved_feed_residue_g_total` to track flow through the dissolution stage but the actual dissolved state is in `dissolved_organic_carbon_mg_c_total` and `dissolved_organic_nitrogen_mg_n_total`. The residue field tracks cumulative throughput and is decremented when mineralization consumes DOC/DON.\n- **Comammox uses AOB's vmax × fraction rather than a separate vmax field**: The spec says \"lower vmax\" — we implement this as `aob_vmax * comammox_vmax_fraction` (default 0.4) rather than an independent absolute vmax, which is functionally equivalent and reduces parameter count.\n- **`emit_once_per_day_pub` wrapper**: To reuse the private `emit_once_per_day` dedup logic from the daily update hook in `engine.rs`, a thin public wrapper was added to `events.rs`. This preserves the existing dedup behavior intact.\n\n## Testing\n- **`cycling_seeded_vs_unseeded`**: Seeded tank reaches low TAN/nitrite faster than unseeded. Unseeded shows non-zero TAN and nitrite peaks.\n- **`filter_cleaning_setback`**: Verifies AOB/NOB biomass decreases after filter cleaning, and TAN rises when feeding resumes.\n- **`limiter_correctness_no_negative_pools`**: Extreme scenario (50g feed, zero DO, zero microbes) — all pools remain finite and non-negative after 100 hours.\n- **`siphon_detritus_reduces_cycling_pressure`**: Siphoning reduces particulate detritus without directly removing dissolved TAN/nitrite/nitrate.\n- **`nitrification_lowers_alkalinity_and_ph`**: Active nitrification produces lower alkalinity and pH than an identical non-nitrifying control, with pH remaining in [5.5, 8.5].\n- **`feed_pulse_tan_concentration_scales_with_volume`**: Peak TAN mg/L in 10L is ≥5× the 100L peak after the same feed pulse.\n- **`event_generation_warm_overfed_weak_aeration`**: Warm (30°C), overfed (3g/day × 14 days), weak-aeration tank emits AmmoniaWarning or OxygenDip with non-empty cause_codes.\n- **`save_load_with_active_cycle_state`**: Save/load determinism verified with active microbe and filter state.\n- **`cycling_fixtures_are_deterministic_and_differ_in_seeding`**: Fixtures are deterministic with same seed, differ only in microbe/filter state.\n- **All 48 tests pass** including all loop-1 through loop-3 regressions (determinism, save/load resume, water change mass balance, thermal response, ambient temperature, dissolved oxygen, chemistry pH drift, threshold events).","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"86001031-e08b-4ab4-a078-b934bda46f61","total_cost_usd":6.642806949999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":87,"cache_creation_input_tokens":123612,"cache_read_input_tokens":7597909,"output_tokens":78766,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":123612,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":87,"outputTokens":78766,"cacheReadInputTokens":7597909,"cacheCreationInputTokens":123612,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":6.541114499999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":45,"outputTokens":4550,"cacheReadInputTokens":183787,"cacheCreationInputTokens":48415,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.10169244999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOu